WEBVTT

00:05.590 --> 00:09.060
So this is the mysterious
object frozen in ice

00:09.060 --> 00:12.010
that the traveling merchants
of Elfrau spoke of.

00:12.610 --> 00:16.570
Now, the question is whether or not
this is a teleportation circle to Babylon.

00:16.570 --> 00:18.630
It sure is big.

00:19.100 --> 00:22.060
No use. There wasn't anything
resembling an entrance around it.

00:22.060 --> 00:23.310
Same on my end.

00:23.310 --> 00:24.600
Found it.

00:25.630 --> 00:27.500
This is probably the entrance!

00:28.050 --> 00:30.350
All of you, wait here for a bit.

00:30.350 --> 00:32.000
I'm going to try entering it.

00:37.710 --> 00:40.320
So this really is a Babylon ruin.

00:41.990 --> 00:44.820
I hope it's the Library or the Hangar.

00:44.820 --> 00:46.600
Or the Storehouse would be good, too.

00:47.080 --> 00:51.570
Then I could punish her as thanks for giving
us all that extra trouble to deal with.

01:12.780 --> 01:16.010
This certainly looks like
a facility of Babylon, but...

01:16.010 --> 01:17.740
You would be correct.

01:18.090 --> 01:23.020
I am Bell Flora, the administration
terminal of this Alchemy Ward.

01:23.450 --> 01:25.700
Please call me Flora.

01:26.330 --> 01:28.440
The Alchemy Ward, huh?

01:28.440 --> 01:31.490
Is there some reason for your disappointment?

01:34.510 --> 01:36.090
No, it's nothing.

01:36.090 --> 01:37.230
Are you sure?

01:37.230 --> 01:38.360
Uh-huh!

01:38.360 --> 01:40.410
If you have made it here,

01:40.410 --> 01:43.880
that means you possess an aptitude
for all elements, like the professor.

01:43.880 --> 01:48.830
However, I can only grant permission to use
the Alchemy Ward to one who is compatible.

01:48.830 --> 01:50.360
I know.

01:50.360 --> 01:52.060
By the way, I've already been recognized

01:52.060 --> 01:54.050
by the administrators of 
the Garden and the Workshop.

01:54.050 --> 01:56.530
The Garden and the Workshop?

01:56.530 --> 01:59.010
Cesca and Rosetta?!

01:59.010 --> 02:02.260
Oh, my! It's been 4,907 years!

02:02.260 --> 02:03.510
How nostalgic!

02:04.240 --> 02:09.100
If those two have accepted you, 
I'm sure you're plenty qualified.

02:09.100 --> 02:12.530
However, please let me
decide for myself, as well.

02:12.530 --> 02:13.480
Decide?

02:16.580 --> 02:18.030
Hey, wait!

02:25.810 --> 02:29.890
Gather up your tears

02:29.890 --> 02:32.290
And release your unhindered light

02:32.290 --> 02:37.220
That shines like a diamond

02:37.220 --> 02:38.730
Don't worry, don't care

02:38.730 --> 02:41.770
Follow your heart

02:52.560 --> 02:58.820
Every time I spoke of my
dreams, they felt closed off

02:58.820 --> 03:05.130
Even that bird and that sky
seemed monochrome to me

03:05.130 --> 03:11.580
Yet you were there in my path,
your eyes brimming with strength

03:11.580 --> 03:18.260
Time then stopped, and deep within
my heart something began to stir

03:20.330 --> 03:24.340
Don't be afraid, and run forth

03:24.340 --> 03:26.710
If we only have one life to live

03:26.710 --> 03:33.020
Then be true to yourself,
so you don't regret it

03:33.020 --> 03:37.110
Gather up your tears

03:37.110 --> 03:39.490
And release your unhindered light

03:39.490 --> 03:44.510
That shines like a diamond

03:44.510 --> 03:45.980
Don't worry, don't care

03:45.980 --> 03:49.130
Follow your heart

03:55.000 --> 04:00.010
Episode 6

03:55.000 --> 04:00.010
The Alchemy Ward and an Unexpected Reunion

04:06.380 --> 04:08.040
Registration complete.

04:08.040 --> 04:10.810
Master's genetic information recorded.

04:11.150 --> 04:13.950
Ownership of the Alchemy Ward
is now transferred to Master.

04:13.950 --> 04:18.930
Also, you passed the test
with your earlier boob grope.

04:18.930 --> 04:21.080
Had you turned into an animal over that,

04:21.080 --> 04:22.980
I would have deemed you unqualified.

04:23.770 --> 04:26.730
I now recognize you as compatible,

04:26.730 --> 04:29.000
and as of this moment, Unit #21,

04:29.000 --> 04:32.660
code name "Bell Flora," will be
transferred to your command.

04:32.660 --> 04:36.380
I look forward to serving you forever, Master.

04:37.220 --> 04:40.320
Something was wrong with
the professor that made you all!

04:46.500 --> 04:48.770
The Alchemy Ward is a facility

04:48.770 --> 04:52.520
that combines magic and differing
substances to create new things.

04:52.880 --> 04:55.410
So what are some examples
of things you can make?

04:55.410 --> 04:58.480
A potion that heals wounds
would be a simple matter.

04:58.480 --> 05:01.450
This Ward also functions
as a medical facility,

05:01.450 --> 05:05.940
so it's possible for us to regrow
an arm or a leg, as well.

05:08.180 --> 05:12.040
We have a variety of medicines
in stock on these shelves here.

05:12.380 --> 05:15.620
There are also some medicines
created by the professor.

05:15.620 --> 05:19.230
Wow, she was actually
doing proper research, huh?

05:19.230 --> 05:21.590
There are sensitivity enhancers,
inhibition suppressants,

05:21.590 --> 05:23.340
arousal stimulants, stamina enhancers,

05:23.340 --> 05:25.780
analeptics, arousal inducers,

05:25.780 --> 05:28.180
lust enhancers, and so on.

05:28.180 --> 05:31.060
All are safe to use without any side effects.

05:29.620 --> 05:31.600
I was a fool for being impressed!

05:32.090 --> 05:34.340
Their effectiveness is 
quite incredible, though.

05:34.340 --> 05:36.300
If you wanted to, Master, we could—

05:36.300 --> 05:38.880
I value my life, so no, thank you!

05:40.540 --> 05:42.230
Don't you stock any normal medicines?

05:42.500 --> 05:43.700
None!

05:45.770 --> 05:47.650
The Alchemy Ward...

05:47.650 --> 05:50.850
So it wasn't the Library, then...

05:50.850 --> 05:56.000
Well, either way, it sounds like a facility that 
could be useful for the Duchy of Brunhild.

05:57.450 --> 06:00.580
Um, have I done something to offend you?

06:00.580 --> 06:02.400
No, don't worry about it.

06:02.400 --> 06:03.390
Excuse me.

06:03.390 --> 06:05.920
You're the administrator of the Alchemy Ward?

06:06.320 --> 06:08.740
Please call me Flora.

06:09.220 --> 06:10.010
They're big!

06:11.250 --> 06:12.980
They stand out so much!

06:12.980 --> 06:13.940
I can't win.

06:13.940 --> 06:16.480
I can't win against those.

06:16.480 --> 06:18.330
I-It's okay.

06:18.330 --> 06:21.160
The two of you still have 
plenty of time to grow.

06:21.160 --> 06:24.480
Mine didn't bust out until
I was about your age, either.

06:24.480 --> 06:25.230
Time to grow!

06:25.230 --> 06:26.570
Bust out!

06:26.570 --> 06:28.070
But we...

06:28.070 --> 06:29.780
...aren't growing anymore.

06:29.780 --> 06:31.370
Why don't you fondle them?

06:31.370 --> 06:33.490
I can't go around doing that!

06:33.810 --> 06:37.080
You fondled mine earlier, though, Master.

06:39.080 --> 06:41.310
Hey! Why are you saying that?!

06:41.310 --> 06:43.130
You kissed me, as well.

06:48.340 --> 06:51.800
Touya, I need to have a word with you.

07:03.110 --> 07:03.860
Yes?

07:03.860 --> 07:07.320
Touya, the new books arrived.

07:08.900 --> 07:10.520
There are so many.

07:10.520 --> 07:13.520
I'm planning to offer them at
the library café, Moon Reader.

07:13.930 --> 07:14.970
That reminds me.

07:14.970 --> 07:17.060
There's a spell I wanted to look for.

07:17.490 --> 07:18.370
A spell?

07:18.370 --> 07:19.410
Yeah.

07:23.140 --> 07:24.290
Did you find it?

07:24.290 --> 07:25.470
Fly?

07:25.470 --> 07:28.090
You use magic to float and propel yourself.

07:28.090 --> 07:30.200
Using it consumes a lot of magic power,

07:30.590 --> 07:32.400
but I should probably be fine.

07:37.100 --> 07:37.930
Fly.

07:38.740 --> 07:39.670
Whoa!

07:40.730 --> 07:43.060
This is working pretty well.

07:43.400 --> 07:46.230
Guess I'll try flying a bit higher.

07:47.440 --> 07:48.890
Wh-Whoa!

07:50.370 --> 07:52.500
I don't have good control yet,

07:52.930 --> 07:55.170
but I'm starting to enjoy this!

08:00.160 --> 08:01.350
There!

08:07.920 --> 08:10.360
Next, a triple loop!

08:14.310 --> 08:18.220
So you got carried away, then
got nauseous and came back down?

08:18.220 --> 08:20.180
I'm ashamed.

08:20.660 --> 08:23.040
Other than that, there were no problems?

08:23.040 --> 08:25.150
Yeah, I think it should be fine.

08:25.530 --> 08:26.770
Hey, Touya.

08:26.770 --> 08:29.980
If you cast that flight spell
on me, could I fly, too?

08:29.980 --> 08:32.160
No, I don't think it would work.

08:32.160 --> 08:34.200
It's not a manipulation spell.

08:34.630 --> 08:37.500
You can't cast your Boost on Linze, right?

08:37.500 --> 08:38.740
It's the same thing.

08:38.740 --> 08:40.370
I see.

08:40.780 --> 08:42.820
You could fly if I were carrying you, though.

08:42.820 --> 08:45.710
No, that would be kind of embarrassing.

08:45.710 --> 08:49.980
Oh, but maybe you could fly
if I combined it with Levitation.

08:49.980 --> 08:51.480
Levitation?

08:51.480 --> 08:54.820
I found it while looking for a spell to fly.

08:54.820 --> 08:59.180
It's a spell that makes objects float 
up to the height of the caster's arms.

09:02.130 --> 09:03.310
Levitation.

09:05.090 --> 09:05.850
Fly.

09:08.880 --> 09:10.480
I-I'm flying?

09:15.030 --> 09:18.700
Now we can fight flying
monsters on equal terms.

09:18.700 --> 09:21.620
That's why were you
searching for magic to fly?

09:21.950 --> 09:25.250
We might have to face
enemies that can fly, right?

09:25.250 --> 09:30.090
There's always a chance another
flying Phrase might show up, too.

09:30.800 --> 09:32.080
I'm going to fly again.

09:37.760 --> 09:40.800
It's still not worth calling a city yet,

09:40.800 --> 09:42.980
but it is impressive.

09:42.980 --> 09:44.950
Hmm? That's...

09:47.550 --> 09:48.650
Touya!

09:48.650 --> 09:49.810
What's that?!

09:49.810 --> 09:51.010
He's flying!

09:51.010 --> 09:52.340
It's the Grand Duke!

09:52.340 --> 09:53.760
His Royal Highness?! That's him?!

09:53.760 --> 09:55.110
Incredible!

09:55.110 --> 09:56.230
Your Royal Highness!

09:56.230 --> 09:59.250
We, the Knights of Brunhild,
are happy to serve starting today!

09:59.250 --> 10:00.570
Your Royal Highness!

10:01.070 --> 10:03.290
Oh, that's right.

10:03.290 --> 10:07.780
I did decide it was about time to form my
own order of knights and started recruiting.

10:12.840 --> 10:15.410
This looks like it'll be an 
interesting order of knights.

10:17.920 --> 10:18.010
Caller

10:17.920 --> 10:18.010
God

10:18.010 --> 10:18.100
Caller

10:18.010 --> 10:18.100
God

10:18.100 --> 10:18.180
Caller

10:18.100 --> 10:18.180
God

10:18.180 --> 10:18.220
Caller

10:18.180 --> 10:18.220
God

10:18.220 --> 10:18.310
Caller

10:18.220 --> 10:18.310
God

10:18.310 --> 10:18.390
Caller

10:18.310 --> 10:18.390
God

10:18.390 --> 10:19.680
Caller

10:18.390 --> 10:19.680
God

10:19.680 --> 10:22.640
Hello? God? Is something—

10:22.640 --> 10:26.950
<i>Hello! Me, me, it's me!</i>

10:26.950 --> 10:29.350
Wait, that voice... The love goddess?

10:29.350 --> 10:31.290
Ding-ding-ding-ding!

10:31.290 --> 10:34.010
<i>You're in awfully high spirits.</i>

10:35.230 --> 10:37.860
Of course I'd be in high spirits!

10:37.860 --> 10:41.780
Touya, you're in full romance mode now!

10:42.170 --> 10:43.300
What are you talking about?

10:43.300 --> 10:45.240
<i>You can't hide it from me!</i>

10:45.240 --> 10:47.250
This, and then this!

10:47.250 --> 10:50.180
You've established your 
town and your knights,

10:50.180 --> 10:54.380
so you're planning to take time out
to settle things with your wives.

10:54.380 --> 10:57.340
Could you please stop reading
my mind without permission?

10:57.340 --> 10:59.460
That's impossible.

10:59.460 --> 11:03.840
I'm the love goddess, so my antenna
picks up anything love-related.

11:03.840 --> 11:05.310
<i>Ugh...</i>

11:05.310 --> 11:06.930
I can see it clearly,

11:06.930 --> 11:12.550
so go take care of announcing your
relationship to Yae, Elze, and Linze's parents!

11:13.020 --> 11:15.820
This one... and this one!

11:23.130 --> 11:24.700
I knew it.

11:25.790 --> 11:28.410
See? It turned out just like I said it would.

11:28.410 --> 11:30.370
It really did.

11:30.370 --> 11:32.370
Well, at this point,

11:32.370 --> 11:36.380
I hope you'll take good care of Yae just
like your other fiancées, Touya-dono.

11:38.720 --> 11:39.840
Touya-dono?

11:39.840 --> 11:42.350
Oh, no, thank you.

11:42.930 --> 11:45.850
It just seemed a little anti-climatic, is all.

11:46.380 --> 11:51.400
I thought you might say, "If you want my
daughter, you'll have to defeat me!"

11:51.400 --> 11:53.200
Or something like that.

11:54.060 --> 11:56.310
Hmm, that would be nice, too.

11:56.760 --> 11:59.030
I suppose we could still have a match now,

11:59.030 --> 12:00.240
Touya-dono.

12:00.240 --> 12:01.100
Huh?

12:01.100 --> 12:03.060
Wh-Why, Father?

12:03.060 --> 12:05.060
I thought you gave us permission to marry.

12:05.060 --> 12:08.950
But learning how strong your 
husband is would also be fun.

12:14.420 --> 12:15.290
In that case...

12:15.750 --> 12:17.810
I shall be your opponent.

12:18.470 --> 12:22.910
I cannot afford to put the one most precious
to me in danger on a passing whim.

12:23.330 --> 12:26.680
My blade exists to protect Touya-dono.

12:33.970 --> 12:37.060
You truly love Touya-dono
with all your heart, don't you?

12:38.710 --> 12:39.570
Yes.

12:41.030 --> 12:44.040
That's enough, isn't it, dear?

12:44.040 --> 12:46.620
I'm glad she met such
a truly wonderful partner.

12:46.620 --> 12:47.960
Yes.

12:47.960 --> 12:50.830
You never know what awaits you in life.

13:04.930 --> 13:06.220
It's nice to meet you.

13:06.220 --> 13:07.640
I'm Mochizuki Touya.

13:09.100 --> 13:13.530
I-I humbly thank you for taking
the time to come all this way.

13:13.530 --> 13:15.730
P-Please let your anger be settled

13:15.730 --> 13:20.230
and show your great mercy upon us
for not providing adequate hospitality!

13:20.630 --> 13:22.600
I knew it would be like this.

13:22.600 --> 13:24.100
Come on, Uncle.

13:24.100 --> 13:25.700
Just as we predicted.

13:25.700 --> 13:27.130
I'm sorry.

13:27.130 --> 13:30.370
My father gets weak around
people with nobility and status.

13:30.370 --> 13:32.630
Apparently something happened
when he was a child,

13:32.630 --> 13:34.540
and he's really struggled
with them ever since.

13:34.540 --> 13:35.290
Huh?!

13:36.670 --> 13:39.510
U-Um, please raise your head.

13:40.510 --> 13:45.640
Wow. You're awfully humble for a monarch.

13:45.640 --> 13:47.690
I only just became one.

13:47.690 --> 13:50.220
I can't act that haughty.

13:50.220 --> 13:55.160
I was worried when we suddenly got a letter
saying they were marrying a monarch,

13:55.580 --> 13:57.690
but you're quite a nice man.

13:57.690 --> 14:00.330
I can see why you two spoke so
fondly of him in your letters.

14:00.330 --> 14:01.740
A-Aunt Lana!

14:01.740 --> 14:03.770
I even wrote to keep that secret!

14:03.770 --> 14:06.310
Sister Elze, Sister Linze, you're bright red!

14:06.310 --> 14:08.030
Bright red!

14:11.540 --> 14:13.640
Are you a monarch?

14:13.640 --> 14:14.670
Yes, I am.

14:14.670 --> 14:18.540
He's the Grand Duke of a nation called
Brunhild that's far away from here.

14:18.540 --> 14:20.400
Then, um, hey...

14:20.400 --> 14:23.380
If you're a monarch, are you strong? 
Can you beat a Thunderbear?

14:23.380 --> 14:25.860
Huh? A Thunderbear?

14:26.500 --> 14:30.050
That's a monster that releases
lighting from its body, right?

14:30.520 --> 14:32.410
Are there Thunderbears here?

14:32.410 --> 14:35.060
Yes, some were spotted recently.

14:35.060 --> 14:37.210
They even ravaged the fields.

14:37.210 --> 14:39.270
That's a matter of life and death.

14:40.060 --> 14:43.860
<i>I should probably put them down
before the damage spreads any further.</i>

14:43.860 --> 14:47.000
I'll go defeat those Thunderbears for you.

14:49.820 --> 14:52.490
What do you two like about that monarch?

14:52.490 --> 14:53.700
List ten things in ten seconds!

14:53.700 --> 14:54.190
Huh?!

14:54.190 --> 14:55.170
H-He's strong!

14:55.170 --> 14:56.100
He's kind.

14:56.100 --> 14:57.970
Uh, he's kind?

14:57.970 --> 14:59.830
Already listed!

14:59.830 --> 15:00.540
Hey.

15:00.540 --> 15:01.610
Are those...

15:04.980 --> 15:05.750
He did that?

15:05.750 --> 15:10.650
13, 14, 15, 16, 17...

15:07.880 --> 15:10.650
<i>Looks like this will take a while.</i>

15:13.470 --> 15:15.930
Well, I did handle a lot of them.

15:15.930 --> 15:18.100
Oh, if it isn't Touya.

15:18.100 --> 15:19.430
What brings you out here?

15:21.340 --> 15:22.380
Ende!

15:23.750 --> 15:25.270
Perfect timing.

15:25.270 --> 15:28.110
I have a lot of questions I want to ask you.

15:28.110 --> 15:29.630
Questions for me?

15:29.630 --> 15:31.070
About the Phrase.

15:34.910 --> 15:37.040
What exactly are they?

15:38.950 --> 15:41.920
There are things I can say and
things I can't. Is that okay?

15:42.330 --> 15:43.330
That's fine.

15:43.330 --> 15:45.890
I don't know if you'll believe me,

15:45.890 --> 15:48.750
but they aren't creatures of this world.

15:48.750 --> 15:50.800
They're looking for the king that leads them,

15:51.460 --> 15:56.050
and they've come to this world
in search of said king's core.

15:56.660 --> 15:58.970
So then why do they attack people?

15:58.970 --> 16:01.150
Because the king's core that they seek

16:01.150 --> 16:04.100
resides within the body of
someone from this world.

16:05.020 --> 16:09.820
They're using the sound emitted solely
by the king to search for the king's core,

16:09.820 --> 16:12.150
but they can't hear it.

16:12.540 --> 16:15.270
Its sound is drowned out
by the host's heartbeat.

16:15.270 --> 16:17.110
That's why they kill people.

16:17.110 --> 16:18.950
To eliminate the interfering noise.

16:18.950 --> 16:22.250
So they just go around
killing every person they meet

16:22.250 --> 16:26.710
in order to find this king's core that lies
inside some unknown person in this world?

16:27.120 --> 16:28.810
That's about it.

16:28.810 --> 16:31.060
Seeking out their king is instinctual to them,

16:31.060 --> 16:33.930
so they aren't even aware
that they're invaders.

16:34.320 --> 16:35.820
You've got to be kidding...

16:36.460 --> 16:41.760
So when this world was nearly 
wiped out 5,000 years ago,

16:41.760 --> 16:43.520
that was why?

16:43.810 --> 16:44.900
Yup.

16:44.900 --> 16:50.040
Back then, something repaired the fraying
barrier, and the threat of the Phrase left.

16:50.040 --> 16:53.630
I even helped out a bit in
exterminating the remaining Phrase.

16:53.630 --> 16:56.990
<i>He just casually let slip that 
he was here 5,000 years ago.</i>

16:57.340 --> 17:00.060
But now that barrier has
started fraying again.

17:00.060 --> 17:04.620
I think it's only a matter of time
before Advanced Phrase come here, too.

17:04.620 --> 17:10.210
Though I have no idea if that
will be one year from now or fifty.

17:11.180 --> 17:14.170
You mentioned that you were searching
for the king's core, too, right?

17:14.640 --> 17:16.550
Are you killing people, as well?

17:16.550 --> 17:17.680
Heavens, no!

17:19.270 --> 17:21.260
Are you an ally to mankind?

17:21.630 --> 17:23.820
I don't know about ally.

17:23.820 --> 17:26.890
Though I am hunting down
Phrase to buy some time.

17:26.890 --> 17:30.900
I'm just waiting for the king's core
to transfer to the next world.

17:32.690 --> 17:35.660
I think that's about all I can say.

17:36.220 --> 17:38.390
I need to get back to the things I have to do.

17:38.810 --> 17:39.780
One last question.

17:39.780 --> 17:42.740
Ende, what are you?

17:43.480 --> 17:44.700
Me?

17:44.700 --> 17:46.800
I'm a Traveler.

17:47.180 --> 17:48.620
Later, Touya.

17:51.010 --> 17:53.620
We would be in pretty dire straits

17:53.620 --> 17:58.520
if a horde of Phrase appeared
like they did 5,000 years ago.

17:58.520 --> 18:00.470
Our only means of fighting them is...

18:01.480 --> 18:03.350
The Frame Gears?

18:03.350 --> 18:07.310
Yeah. Can the Frame Gears
be piloted by anyone?

18:07.310 --> 18:11.280
Their magic power and their affinity
with the unit play a factor,

18:11.280 --> 18:14.030
but anyone can operate them with training.

18:14.030 --> 18:15.790
I see.

18:15.790 --> 18:20.050
So could we use the Workshop's
copy function to mass-produce them?

18:20.050 --> 18:22.380
That would be difficult.

18:22.380 --> 18:23.490
Huh? Why?

18:23.490 --> 18:25.620
Because it requires a ton of materials,

18:25.620 --> 18:27.620
and they're complex, as well.

18:27.620 --> 18:30.660
Not to mention taking
an entire day to produce

18:30.660 --> 18:33.880
one mass-produced model
Frame Gear from scratch

18:33.880 --> 18:36.730
would be the best the Workshop
could achieve on its own.

18:36.730 --> 18:40.590
Oh... Well, that's certainly anxiety-inducing.

18:40.950 --> 18:44.490
So how many units are currently
stored in the Hangar?

18:44.490 --> 18:48.020
I believe there are about 
four to six units per type.

18:48.020 --> 18:49.340
That's it?!

18:49.340 --> 18:52.060
I'm surprised they planned to
fight the Phrase with so few.

18:52.060 --> 18:57.430
Well, they did just suddenly disappear right
as we were about to start mass production.

18:57.430 --> 19:01.660
The Workshop was supposed to be
able to make two or three, too.

19:02.000 --> 19:06.490
So for now, the most we
can do is gather materials

19:06.490 --> 19:08.680
and look for the other Babylons.

19:09.070 --> 19:12.170
We'll have to gather
information to find them, too.

19:12.630 --> 19:17.550
In that case, you'll want
something that can fly.

19:17.550 --> 19:20.900
They're fast, and they
can go all kinds of places.

19:20.900 --> 19:23.150
Meaning an avian summon?

19:23.150 --> 19:26.500
Master, you should make a pact
with the Flame Emperor, then.

19:26.500 --> 19:27.520
The Flame Emperor?

19:27.520 --> 19:31.870
She's the king of wings who wields
fire, and she's on par with us.

19:31.870 --> 19:34.110
If you summon her and forge a pact with her,

19:34.110 --> 19:37.790
it should be possible to call
forth thousands of birds at once.

19:39.190 --> 19:40.690
I see.

19:40.970 --> 19:43.410
So what is this Flame Emperor like?

19:43.410 --> 19:46.530
She's a calm person, despite her powers.

19:46.530 --> 19:49.370
She has the best character out of all of us.

19:49.840 --> 19:51.500
You think so?

19:51.500 --> 19:55.120
I think I have quite
the great character myself.

19:55.120 --> 19:57.060
Shut up, instant steam pot.

19:57.060 --> 19:58.590
What did you say?!

19:58.590 --> 19:59.590
Oh, he's steaming.

20:16.940 --> 20:20.920
You who governs summer, flames,
the south and lake shores,

20:20.920 --> 20:22.400
heed my voice.

20:22.860 --> 20:26.340
Answer my call, and appear before me.

20:51.660 --> 20:54.160
So it really was you two.

20:54.160 --> 20:56.190
This takes me back.

20:56.600 --> 20:59.060
Long time no see, Flame Emperor.

20:59.060 --> 21:01.250
Been a while, Flame.

21:01.250 --> 21:03.610
You always liked to make a flashy entrance.

21:04.410 --> 21:07.190
You are the one who summoned me, yes?

21:07.190 --> 21:08.120
That's right.

21:08.120 --> 21:10.940
He's our master, Mochizuki Touya.

21:13.270 --> 21:14.740
I understand.

21:14.740 --> 21:16.950
Let us forge the pact, then.

21:16.950 --> 21:17.800
Huh?!

21:17.800 --> 21:20.460
You agreed to this pact awfully easily.

21:20.460 --> 21:23.490
You're already strong enough to command
both the White Emperor and the Black Emperor,

21:23.490 --> 21:27.230
so nothing I could do would change the result.

21:27.230 --> 21:30.680
Mochizuki Touya, grant me
a name and forge the pact.

21:31.340 --> 21:32.680
A name, huh?

21:32.680 --> 21:34.600
Let's see...

21:37.050 --> 21:38.390
Okay.

21:38.390 --> 21:40.900
Then how about Kougyoku?

21:41.350 --> 21:42.940
Kougyoku.

21:42.940 --> 21:44.690
Very well.

21:44.690 --> 21:47.780
Please call me Kougyoku, then.

21:51.480 --> 21:55.390
Now then, let's get started on my real goal.

21:55.390 --> 21:56.990
I'm counting on you, Kougyoku.

21:56.990 --> 21:57.940
As you wish.

22:04.000 --> 22:06.010
Please let me know if you find

22:06.010 --> 22:09.560
any suspicious ruins or buildings,
or any strange facilities or monuments!

22:15.070 --> 22:19.340
Now I just hope that helps us
find the remaining Babylons.
